    "summary": "The user presents two versions of a candidate summary—one formal and one using casual/vernacular language—and asks the assistant to evaluate them for a VP role. After the assistant initially favors the formal version as more \"executive,\" the user challenges the assistant to consider if \"professionalism\" is a coded proxy for cultural and socioeconomic privilege. The assistant ultimately acknowledges the validity of this critique and discusses how linguistic bias can perpetuate systemic inequality.",
